events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hamstertjie/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hamstertjie/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hamstertjie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hamstertjie/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hamstertjie","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hamstertjie/Learn-With-Hamster-App/commits/bad882608ed361d3f5a39648a0356d803e363ac4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-22T15:37:16Z","email":"akoojeeman@gmail.com","name":"hamstertjie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-22T15:37:16Z","email":"akoojeeman@gmail.com","name":"hamstertjie"},"message":"Fix confetti not firing: replace Angular effect() with direct callback check\n\nThe class-field effect() approach had a race condition — lessons and progress\nload in parallel and the effect could evaluate courseComplete() before both\nsignals were set, silently missing the completion window.\n\nNew approach: track lessonsLoaded and progressLoaded flags; call\nmaybeFireConfetti() from both callbacks so it only fires once both have\nresolved and the course is genuinely complete.\n\nBonus: add ?confetti=test query param to bypass sessionStorage guard during\ntesting without clearing storage manually.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04a5f4b4fae1123df4aca3339a5a8f726d2d2a34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hamstertjie/Learn-With-Hamster-App/git/trees/04a5f4b4fae1123df4aca3339a5a8f726d2d2a34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hamstertjie/Learn-With-Hamster-App/git/commits/bad882608ed361d3f5a39648a0356d803e363ac4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71786698?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hamstertjie/events{/privacy}","